         "description": "The power steering system must vary the steering torque sensing to facilitate maneuverability at low speeds and stability at high speeds.",
         "implications": [
            "At low speeds, the system should provide increased steering assistance to enhance maneuverability, making it easier for drivers to navigate tight spaces or make sharp turns.",
            "At higher speeds, the system should reduce steering assistance to ensure greater vehicle stability, preventing oversteer and maintaining control during high-speed maneuvers."
         ],
         "considerations": [
            "The system must have a mechanism to detect vehicle speed and adjust steering torque accordingly.",
            "Calibration of the power steering system is crucial to balance between maneuverability at low speeds and stability at high speeds."
         ]
      },
      {  
         "ID": 15,
         "description": "The system must log all steering angle sensor errors and issues for diagnostics and maintenance purposes.",
         "implications": [
            "A comprehensive logging mechanism should be in place to capture any anomalies or faults detected by the steering angle sensors.",
            "Logs should include timestamps, error codes, and contextual data to aid in diagnosing issues."
         ],
         "considerations": [
            "The system must ensure that logs are stored securely and can be accessed easily for maintenance purposes.",
            "Regular updates and checks on the logging system may be necessary to maintain its accuracy and reliability."
         ]
      },
      {  
         "ID": 87,
         "description": "Upon corner exit, the system must ensure smooth power delivery and vehicle stability based on the interplay between the steering angle sensing and the acceleration sensing.",
         "implications": [
            "The system should dynamically adjust power delivery to maintain traction and control as the vehicle exits a turn.",
            "Integration of steering angle data with acceleration inputs is necessary to predict and respond to potential loss of stability."
         ],
         "considerations": [
            "Real-time processing capabilities are required to analyze sensor data and make immediate adjustments.",
            "The system should be tested under various driving conditions to ensure consistent performance during corner exits."
         ]
      }
   ]
}

